{"queued timestamp field uses timezone.now() evaluated at import time instead of field(default_factory=timezone.now), causing all AssignmentSource instances to share the same stale timestamp": 0.921899139881134, "Inbound assignee sync does not preserve or forward source metadata into where_should_sync() or other routing logic, only tagging the source on immediate assign/deassign calls": 0.37773388624191284, "If an inbound integration webhook results in a reassignment flow that first deassigns then assigns, the outbound task from the latter step can be queued without a source, allowing the originating integration to see its own outbound update and continue the sync loop": 0.2389899641275406, "Status sync path calls should_sync('outbound_status') and sync_status_outbound without any AssignmentSource context, leaving status-related echo routes unable to suppress propagation back to the originating integration": 0.5187733173370361, "Tests only assert that queued is non-null in to_dict(), so they would not catch the stale-default timestamp bug": 0.8565854430198669, "When reassigning, remove_old_assignees() deassigns the previous user without passing through the new assignment_source, so the outbound deassign path cannot tell the change originated from an integration": 0.2873024344444275, "The deassign path during reassignment can enqueue sync_assignee_outbound with no source context, allowing the initiating integration to receive a deassign/update and continue the sync loop": 0.7342849373817444}